    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d596">

                <pb facs="0639" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.512/67: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Agent and
                        Consul General at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Blake</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-28T18:00:00-05:00">January 28, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. To supplement the Department’s telegram 4, January 22, 6 p.m. The Department
                    of State will refuse consent to the “padlock law”, and instructions are being
                    sent by pouch for the reply to the French Resident General.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
